-- title:
--   Crossing points of the special fibre are not cusps (pole chart)
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and let $K_0$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 (M' * q))`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101), that is, the subfield generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the quotients of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_0(M'q)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with $L$ as its fraction field, with $q$ lying in the maximal ideal of $A$, and let $K_0$ carry a compatible $A$-algebra structure. Let $j \in K_0$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), and let $\varpi \in A$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Write $B$ for [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgInf A K₀ j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L144), the subalgebra of elements of $K_0$ integral over $A[j^{-1}]$. If $y \subseteq B$ is a prime ideal containing the image of $\varpi$, and there are two distinct minimal primes of the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$ in $B$ both contained in $y$, then the element $j^{-1}$ of $B$, namely [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.jInvChartInf A K₀ j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L150), does not lie in $y$.
--
--   This is the pole-chart statement that a point of the special fibre at which two branches of the model of $X_0(M'q)$ over $A$ meet is not a cusp: the two components of the reduction cross only at supersingular points, where $j$ is finite, so $1/j$ cannot vanish there (Deligne–Rapoport, Katz–Mazur). It is used, together with its finite-chart counterpart, in the full-level statements comparing membership in the non-unit locus with membership in the Gauss-type set for $\Gamma_0(M'q)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_jInvChartInf_not_mem_of_exists_two_minimalPrimes_span_le_chartAlgInf_laurentBaseChange_gamma0_mul.lean

